      "old_content": "<!-- wp:table -->\n<figure class=\"wp-block-table\"><table class=\"has-fixed-layout\"><tbody><tr><td><strong>DR. SUN'S CLINICAL PERSPECTIVE</strong><em>\"In my practice, I see patients who have spent months - sometimes years - seeing the wrong type of clinician. They have been told their swelling is \"just water weight\" or a side effect that will pass. By the time they reach a lymphologist, the condition has often progressed further than it needed to. This means for patients that the type of specialist you see first really matters. If your swelling is persistent, asymmetrical, or follows a cancer diagnosis or surgery, ask your GP specifically for a referral to a lymphologist - not just a general physician. Early, accurate diagnosis is the single biggest factor in long-term outcomes.\"</em><strong>- Dr Jeremy Sun, Lymphedema Microsurgery Specialist, Singapore</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<!-- /wp:table -->",
